Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.35,0:00:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.87,0:00:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.45,0:00:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.57,0:00:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Your moves!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.39,0:01:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, this thing ain't\Nbudging, boys and girls.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.07,0:01:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like we're trapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.69,0:01:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, there's got to be\Nanother way out of this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.63,0:01:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But these tunnels run everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.17,0:01:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We could be lost down here forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.87,0:01:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Forever?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.55,0:01:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.95,0:01:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Bakura?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.86,0:01:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Bakura, what gives?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.37,0:01:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems my Millennium Ring is tugging\Nme in this direction. Huh? Why? Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.45,0:01:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi and I think that my\NMillennium Ring can detect other
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.09,0:01:38.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Millennium items And that it's\Nbeen honing in on Pegasus'
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.35,0:01:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Millennium Eye So it could be leading\Nus right to his castle Pegasus,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.45,0:01:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't wait to get my\Nhands on that creep I
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.25,0:01:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,love this show But what's\Nplaying on Dungeon TV?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.89,0:01:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, goody. It's another installment\Nin the sad little saga of Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.11,0:01:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother will come for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.05,0:02:02.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I know he'll come like he always has.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.59,0:02:05.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just you and me now, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.59,0:02:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But it'll be okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.57,0:02:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Like the way he came for me the\Nday Mom and Dad passed away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.79,0:02:12.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.70,0:02:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm scared, Seto. Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.63,0:02:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll always be there for you, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.49,0:02:17.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.81,0:02:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Pegasus thinks that by\Nkeeping me locked away,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.41,0:02:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,he can take over your company, Kybocorp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.67,0:02:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But Pegasus doesn't know you like I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.89,0:02:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,How when we were growing up,\Nyou never lost at anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.95,0:02:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd never give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.25,0:02:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd just keep on going\Nuntil you'd beaten everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.69,0:02:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And you're gonna beat\NPegasus the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.21,0:02:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So come and rescue me, big brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.15,0:02:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.06,0:02:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll always be there for you, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.81,0:02:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.49,0:02:48.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.77,0:02:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So are we getting anywhere, Bakura?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.19,0:02:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's like we've been walking forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.09,0:02:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead of looking like the way\Nout, it seems like a big maze.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.33,0:03:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.24,0:03:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And look at the walls down here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.03,0:03:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,All the rocks are neatly arranged.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.21,0:03:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems man-made.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.89,0:03:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You think someone could\Nbe living down here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.35,0:03:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd have to be mole people.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.67,0:03:13.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at all these corridors.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.89,0:03:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be a dozen different\Ndirections we could go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.13,0:03:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,So now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.59,0:03:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Which way do we go?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.07,0:03:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This way. Huh? Follow me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.45,0:03:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The ring is pulling me this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.51,0:03:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, tell it to pull slower.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.29,0:03:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.20,0:03:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Bakura, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.69,0:03:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Why have you stopped?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.95,0:03:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.57,0:03:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You have entered sacred ground where\Nonly duelists can be found. Yeah
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.45,0:03:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,well we're duelists before you pass
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.29,0:03:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,across this chamber you must agree to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.11,0:04:04.55,Default,,0,0,0,,face the danger so let the contest\Nnow begin notify your next of kin
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.63,0:04:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,you're trapped and the doors are all
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.37,0:04:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,locked you'll face the brothers paradox
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.59,0:04:14.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Employed by Pegasus as Eliminators.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.07,0:04:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,To take all your starship indicators.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.09,0:04:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You gotta duel these goons, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.45,0:04:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And if, by some crazy\Nfluke, you manage to win...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.25,0:04:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Why then, a puzzling new test shall begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.17,0:04:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,For over my shoulder, you'll see a door.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.83,0:04:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And over my brothers, you'll see...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.93,0:04:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,One door more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.21,0:04:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,The test a choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.41,0:04:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,That you must make.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.61,0:04:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Which of these doors will you take?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.11,0:04:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.02,0:04:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,One door leads to an endless maze.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.35,0:04:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Where you will wander all your days.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.57,0:04:47.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The other door's the path you need.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.55,0:04:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Choose correctly and be freed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.41,0:04:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But which door leads out?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.91,0:04:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And which leads to woe?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.41,0:04:53.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That's for you to guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.99,0:04:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And for the brother's paradox to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.77,0:05:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,So even if Yuki wins this match, we could\Nstill wind up lost in those caves forever?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.37,0:05:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Against us, one mere\Nduelist would be grieved.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.09,0:05:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,So you must duel as a team.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.89,0:05:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Two-on-two?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.93,0:05:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Like a tag team?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.17,0:05:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I never heard of anyone\Ndueling like that. Me neither.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.91,0:05:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But I don't think we have\Nmuch of a choice here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.83,0:05:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.39,0:05:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tag team it is, and I'd be honored\Nif Joey would duel by my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:47.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, you got it, bro.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.25,0:05:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you's brothers, Paradox.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.27,0:05:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Me and Yugi are gonna clean your clocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.67,0:05:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to be puzzled.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.21,0:05:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to be fooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.87,0:06:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to be baffled,\Nfor on this field we rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.23,0:06:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna baffle the two of\Nthem if they don't stop rhyming.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.35,0:06:08.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough of your quips.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.69,0:06:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, time to wager star chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.13,0:06:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll throw down two.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.89,0:06:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus four more for a total of six. Agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.07,0:06:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,This is it, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.45,0:06:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,If we play our cards right,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.65,0:06:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,we'll both have enough star chips\Nto gain entrance into the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.65,0:06:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we can finally confront Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.61,0:06:26.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.33,0:06:30.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why Pegasus pays my brother and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.59,0:06:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,To keep you from achieving victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.17,0:06:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, guys, teamwork from here on out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.15,0:06:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.06,0:06:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be the team, you do the work.\NGood luck! Quiet, fools! Time to duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.51,0:06:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,First turn honors are mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.19,0:06:45.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Labyrinth wall!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.81,0:06:47.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.72,0:06:48.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would he play that card?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.07,0:06:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,He doesn't even have any attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.41,0:06:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.37,0:06:56.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, the floor!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.83,0:06:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Something's coming out of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.13,0:07:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Strike that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.21,0:07:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,A whole bunch of things\Nare coming out of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.27,0:07:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,a maze quite right and unless you can\Nnavigate it correctly you'll be lost in his
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.87,0:07:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,passageways forever now\Nno more questions no
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.41,0:07:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,more stalls make your\Nmove the labyrinth calls
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.93,0:07:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,soon pegasus will be sorry for the\Npain he's caused me and my brother
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.31,0:07:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.01,0:07:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Doesn't he realize that nothing\Nwill stop me from getting him back?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.67,0:07:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, he'll soon find out
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.87,0:07:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Make your move, go! Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.83,0:07:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold your horses already!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.59,0:07:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We don't even know how this tag\Nteam thing works It's simple,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.89,0:07:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,we all start with 2,000 life\Npoints like any duel However,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.69,0:08:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,if just one duelist loses those 2,000\Npoints, then his teammate loses with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.91,0:08:05.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, Yugi's putting a lot of faith in me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.35,0:08:06.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't let him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.69,0:08:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The players on each team will alternate\Nturns with every passing round.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.49,0:08:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.47,0:08:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I will play, then Yugi, then my\Nbrother, then Joey, then back to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.65,0:08:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, as for the actual gameplay in the\NLabyrinth Arena, it too is quite simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.57,0:08:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,All monsters you summon during this match\Nwill act like pieces on a game board.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.39,0:08:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,As for moving, each monster can move the\Nnumber of spaces equal to its power level.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.17,0:08:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And while your game pieces are moving,\Nours will be moving too. Finally,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.79,0:08:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,if you somehow manage to get past our\Ncreatures and find your way through the maze,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.91,0:08:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,your reward will be a choice of two doors.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.07,0:08:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Select the correct door and find\Nthe path to freedom and fresh air.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.77,0:08:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Select the wrong door\Nand find only despair.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.09,0:08:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had just about enough of\Nall your lame-brained rhyming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.17,0:08:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And what do you mean, one\Ndoor leads to despair?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.55,0:08:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.79,0:09:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.09,0:09:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll give you a clue.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.63,0:09:05.75,Default,,0,0,0,,While everything one of us\Ntells you shall be true...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.43,0:09:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The other will speak\Nnothing but lies to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.29,0:09:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Truths and lies?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.43,0:09:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What are they talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.87,0:09:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Come now, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.73,0:09:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,it's just a riddle and\Nyou had better solve
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.89,0:09:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,it otherwise you won't\Nsee the light of day or
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.45,0:09:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,your grandpa ever again\Nfrom this point forward
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.15,0:09:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,one of us will speak\Nnothing but the total truth
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.35,0:09:35.51,Default,,0,0,0,,and the other will speak everything\Nbut the truth so you see it is quite
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.59,0:09:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,simple to learn which of the two is\Nthe right door you have only to ask
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.63,0:09:43.05,Default,,0,0,0,,nothing more wait what if you're lying
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.13,0:09:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,To me right now, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.79,0:09:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,i never lie don't
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.15,0:09:54.05,Default,,0,0,0,,be fooled my door is most certainly the\Ndoor that will guarantee you're freed
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.13,0:10:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,liar mine is the door that'll grant\Nsafe passage if they'd only heed wait
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.47,0:10:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,a sec this sounds like an old riddle\Ni know sure the liar the truth teller
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.71,0:10:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,the choosing between two directions\Nlet out the rest of it go hey yugi i
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.09,0:10:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,think i know this riddle it starts\Nwith a fork in the road Check this out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.65,0:10:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,There's this kid trying to get\Nto the village of truth-tellers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.31,0:10:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Thing is, there's a village\Nof liars right next to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.19,0:10:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The kid doesn't know which way to go,\Nso he asks a villager for directions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.55,0:10:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But he doesn't know if the villager's\Nfrom Truthville or Liarsburg.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.95,0:10:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So the villager guy says he'll answer\None question, and that's the riddle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.75,0:10:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What should the kid ask\Nto get to Truthville?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.09,0:10:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,So the kid asks the guy to\Ntake him to his own village.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.35,0:10:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Because a truthful guy\Nwould have to take him to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.29,0:10:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,the village of truth on\Naccount of being truthful.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.17,0:10:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and a liar would have to take\Nhim to the village of truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.83,0:10:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,too, because that'd be lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.27,0:10:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So first, we've got to find out\Nwhich one of you tells the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.75,0:10:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Then proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.79,0:10:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, we'll allow\Nyou each one question.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.23,0:10:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.14,0:10:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,like the kid in the riddle asked\Nthe guy to show him his village,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.17,0:10:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,all I have to do is ask\Nyou to show me your door.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.39,0:11:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So both of you, show me the\Ndoor that you're gone in.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.01,0:11:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the truthful guy will\Nhave to point to his own door
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.99,0:11:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,and the liar will have to\Npoint to the other guy's door.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.07,0:11:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Bingo!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.69,0:11:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, it worked like a charm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.41,0:11:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Hera's the liar and Doc tells the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.55,0:11:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Yugi just has to ask Docs which\Ndoor leaves out of here and we're set.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.85,0:11:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.51,0:11:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That seemed a little too easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.75,0:11:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, Yugi, how about a little\Nsomething for the effort here?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.41,0:11:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate to disappoint you, Joey, but I don't\Nthink we've solved this riddle just yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.57,0:11:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, I think we're going down the\Nwrong road ourselves, so to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.35,0:11:49.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But I told you, Yug, I\Nheard this one before.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.91,0:11:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Your riddle has some things in\Ncommon with our present predicament,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.55,0:11:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,but there are some key differences.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.15,0:11:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And trust me, Joey, those key differences\Nchange the entire nature of the problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.79,0:11:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.03,0:12:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,In your riddle, there was only one\Nperson to question at the crossroads.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.65,0:12:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But in our situation, we have two.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.99,0:12:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,para and dox.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.93,0:12:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, both para and dox have\Ntold us the exact same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.75,0:12:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,One of them will speak
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.25,0:12:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,nothing but the truth, and the\Nother will speak nothing but lies.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.91,0:12:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But there's a problem with that
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.89,0:12:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,already.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.80,0:12:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Because if they were, as they said,\None truth teller and one liar,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.25,0:12:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,the liar could never admit to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.17,0:12:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That would be telling the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.73,0:12:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way they could both make that\Nstatement is if they were both lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.07,0:12:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And that means we can't trust either\NPara, Dox, or their riddle. Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.79,0:12:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My brain hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.99,0:12:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.43,0:12:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That riddle was just meant\Nto throw us off course.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.45,0:12:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's duel now and figure\Nout the door dilemma later.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.53,0:12:48.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice call, Yug.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.67,0:12:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I do all my best problem-solving\Non the field anyways.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.09,0:12:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's win this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.15,0:12:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll have to be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.57,0:13:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never played on a\Nlabyrinth field before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.45,0:13:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.59,0:13:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,with my Beaver Warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.65,0:13:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,A good choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.89,0:13:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,A rat for a maze.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.31,0:13:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But his time's running out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.87,0:13:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the last of his days.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.51,0:13:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.97,0:13:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Beaver, forward four spaces, one\Nfor each of your level points.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.93,0:13:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.31,0:13:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Four spaces and you're already in too far.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.29,0:13:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.83,0:13:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And I am merging Shadow Ghoul into the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.49,0:13:33.95,Default,,0,0,0,,labyrinth wall itself by\Nmeans of polymerization.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.21,0:13:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.49,0:13:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.99,0:13:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Wall shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.65,0:13:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Reaping claw slash!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.89,0:13:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Beaver Warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.39,0:13:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it came out of the wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.93,0:14:00.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's going back where\Nour guys can't get at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.55,0:14:03.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Very lethal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.09,0:14:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,They're cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.09,0:14:07.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It moved too many spaces. On the contrary.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.05,0:14:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The wall shadow didn't move any spaces.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.23,0:14:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It moved on the wall. That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.59,0:14:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And the wall doesn't have any spaces.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.75,0:14:17.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.39,0:14:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Our monsters have to count\Nspaces as they walk the maze,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.35,0:14:23.23,Default,,0,0,0,,while their wall shadow can\Nmove through the maze walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.31,0:14:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And that means he can strike\Nwhen we least expect it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.03,0:14:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,So now you know our strategy is unleashing\Na monster that you cannot see. You fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.63,0:14:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You won't know when the wall\Nshadow's about to land a blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.45,0:14:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.37,0:14:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Axe Raider in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.57,0:14:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll also place one other\Ncard face down on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.75,0:14:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,But since I can't see your shifty\Nlittle monster, I can't attack it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.51,0:14:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,So I won't advance at all this turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.21,0:14:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll just keep Axe Raider as far away from
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.57,0:15:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,the wall and your Sneaky\NWeasel as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.25,0:15:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll still be ready to\Nattack at any moment. Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.23,0:15:06.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.14,0:15:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a good move, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.35,0:15:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as you keep\Nfar away from the wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.87,0:15:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,you can avoid any sneak\Nattack by the wall shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.79,0:15:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So far, so good.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.51,0:15:16.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't cost us any life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.93,0:15:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Good move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.84,0:15:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope Joey can keep this up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.99,0:15:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't sweat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.97,0:15:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,With Yugi as his partner, Joey can't lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.47,0:15:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.27,0:15:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,This tag team stuff is\Ntricky because they can
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.95,0:15:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,focus on attacking the\Nweakest duelists first.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.37,0:15:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.69,0:15:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,My turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.81,0:15:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And I lay this card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.87,0:15:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Jirai Gumo.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.95,0:15:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Any opposing monster that\Nsteps on the space with Jirai
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.47,0:15:45.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Gumo's symbol will instantly fall\Nvictim to its fatal surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.97,0:15:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll also lay the labyrinth tank in attack\Nmode and move it forward seven spaces.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.83,0:16:00.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Good job, brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.27,0:16:02.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That should help trap\Nthem within our maze.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.53,0:16:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, brother. It's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.57,0:16:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I play the Celtic Guardian in attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.11,0:16:15.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Advance four paces into the maze.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.57,0:16:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But the Celtic Guardian's attack strength\Nis much lower than that of Wall Shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.57,0:16:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he'll be wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.41,0:16:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.79,0:16:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.71,0:16:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you not learn anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.23,0:16:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Wall Shadow, attack Celtic Guardian, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.47,0:16:38.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Guardian is doomed and\Nyour life points with it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.51,0:16:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Hm, I'm afraid not.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.25,0:16:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean, kunai with chain?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.41,0:16:50.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.47,0:16:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,My trap card worked!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.07,0:16:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Reel him in, Axe Raider!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.53,0:17:01.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The card I played face down before\Nwas a trap card, kunai with chain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.99,0:17:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It captures any opponent that attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.17,0:17:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I laid that trap card to help Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.23,0:17:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It raised the Celtic\NGuardian's attack power by 500.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.17,0:17:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,putting its strength\Nhigher than Wall Shadows.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.67,0:17:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Celtic Guardian, attack Wall Shadow!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.59,0:17:19.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So now it's lights out\Nfor your shadow. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.31,0:17:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Wall Shadow is beaten!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.33,0:17:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What a team!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.63,0:17:28.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, they're working together\Nto beat those wacky brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.93,0:17:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's really getting to\Nbe a much better player.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.45,0:17:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,He's thinking strategically.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.23,0:17:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.14,0:17:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,To stop our decline,\Nthese two we must halt!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.51,0:17:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't look at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.67,0:17:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not my fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.17,0:17:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,If we keep this up,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.61,0:17:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,we'll win this double duel and have\Nenough starships to enter the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.07,0:17:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Teamwork, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.25,0:17:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, but we haven't won yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.99,0:17:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to keep on our guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.63,0:17:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,if we're going to beat the\NParadox Brothers and win
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.45,0:17:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,our way out of this twisted\Nunderground labyrinth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.03,0:18:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,A toast to Yugi for winning the first round\Nwith the help of his little pal, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.91,0:18:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Pegasus,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.93,0:18:09.93,Default,,0,0,0,,a thousand pardons for\Ninterrupting your greatness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.19,0:18:13.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm growing tired of your\Nconstant interruptions, Croquet.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.81,0:18:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you'd want to know Seto\NKaiba's been spotted on the island.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.37,0:18:19.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I already know that, Croquet.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.39,0:18:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you, the head of my security,\Nalways the last to learn these things?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.97,0:18:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.01,0:18:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba will come to us after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.83,0:18:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,We have the bait.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.81,0:18:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,What's happened to you, brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.67,0:18:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Why haven't you come?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.09,0:18:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You said you'd always be here for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.55,0:18:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.99,0:18:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You never failed me before.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.37,0:18:47.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Give it back! Give it to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.49,0:18:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I give, I give!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.23,0:18:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, Mokuba. Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.41,0:19:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You always come through for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.79,0:19:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So where are you now, Seto?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.95,0:19:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Why haven't you found me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.77,0:19:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.15,0:19:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Why haven't you stopped Pegasus?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.45,0:19:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.15,0:19:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming to save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.63,0:19:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And if Pegasus tries to get in\Nmy way, he'll live to regret it.
